    "held": "First two correct clickable current inventory tiles registered in assistant pixels. Complete checks both tiles in final positions after full recognition and excludes preview-only pixels.",
    "comparisons": "Paired trials against frozen baseline using identical samples, fresh isolated state and real Windows capture, FP32 models and Qt. The busy and moving-lead-in cohorts exercise distinct conditions.",
    "limits": "Repeated plays of one continuous reward-to-map transition on one Windows machine. No live game was attached. Full inventory latency on a naturally recorded contiguous transition remains unverified."
  },
  "shipped": [
    "Main capture requests native updates every 33 ms and spaces full callback processing at 100 ms outside the lock; closing wakes its session.",
    "Prepared GPU map OCR can overlap canonical direction batches on CPU with recognition of the previous batch, preserving corrections, row order and widths.",
    "After current held-card names are confirmed, expanded-bar icon matching and resource OCR can overlap. Resource signals retain order and new-frame priority crosses the icon worker boundary."
  ],
